{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Cross-note from a453 RCA (/rebar-debug Phase 1)\n\nRoot-caused the shared tickets-store growth driver on `defensive-buckskin-rhino` a453. Summary relevant to this data-disk alarm:\n\n**Shared driver:** a ~10× step-change surge in `tickets`-branch commits from **2026-08-21** (~120K commits — over half the 235,260-commit branch — in 8 days), dominated (88% of non-merge events) by the **enrichment quartet** (ENQUEUE/CLAIM/DONE_ENRICH + TICKET_DIGEST), fanned ~4–5× per ticket edit + 27K auto-reconcile merges, all permanently retained (no causal-stability GC; compaction only renames to `.retired`). 1,239 tickets re-enriched ~15×.\n\n**Where 5a05 DIFFERS from a453:** a453's CI metric is a **blobless** pack (~90% trees, 0 blobs). This **on-disk** store is **larger and blob-inclusive** — it also carries f9ee's ~235 MB comment-echo blob bloat + `.bridge_state` churn + working-tree/`.retired` retained files that the blobless CI pack excludes. So the data-disk growth = **the same commit/tree surge PLUS the blob mass**.\n\n**Timing:** the acute 08-26 climb to 88% is ~5 days after the 08-21 surge — consistent with sustained fill crossing the alarm threshold. A possible **independent component** (Gerrit review artifacts / server-side packs sharing this volume) is plausible but **unverifiable read-only**; not chased (root-disk pressure is separate/resolved).\n\n**Remediation** (handed back, not implemented): bound enrichment fan-out (`apparent-sighted-cockatoo` 4520 — prevents future growth), reclaim retained history (`polite-antivirus-bedbug` 536b causal-stability GC or a one-time rewrite like `censual-organic-mouflon` — the only directions that *shrink* on-disk mass), footprint budget (`epidemic-chocolaty-imago` 0754). Full RCA + ranked directions on a453."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788027479716549620,"uuid":"6ab947a0-c1e1-4417-b9dd-fdb3e1c673dc"}